      <section id="about" class="section about-section"><div class="container">
        <div class="section-intro reveal"><p class="kicker">The workshop</p><h2>Understanding markets<br /><span>in a changing world.</span></h2></div>
        <div class="about-layout reveal"><p class="large-copy">Artificial intelligence is reshaping how financial markets are designed, analyzed and operated. New venues, new assets and new forms of automation are opening questions at the frontier of market microstructure.</p><div><p>From centralized exchanges to decentralized protocols, trading, liquidity provision, price formation and information flow remain central challenges. This workshop brings the communities working on these questions into the same room.</p><p>Through invited talks, contributed presentations, panels and interactive sessions, we will explore machine learning, reinforcement learning, agent-based modelling and other data-driven methods for modern financial systems.</p></div></div>
      </div></section>

      <section id="topics" class="section topics-section"><div class="container">
        <div class="section-intro reveal"><p class="kicker">Research directions</p><h2>Topics of <span>interest.</span></h2><p class="section-note">Explore the questions at the intersection of AI, market microstructure and modern financial systems.</p></div>
        <div class="topic-accordion reveal">
          <details open><summary><strong>AI agents for trading</strong><i>+</i></summary><p>Learning, reasoning and acting in complex market environments, from autonomous trading agents to multi-agent simulations.</p></details>
          <details><summary><strong>Liquidity and market making</strong><i>+</i></summary><p>How intelligent agents provide and consume liquidity, and how AI can improve market making and liquidity provision.</p></details>
          <details><summary><strong>Price discovery and optimal execution</strong><i>+</i></summary><p>New methods for forecasting, routing, execution and understanding information flow in automated markets.</p></details>
          <details><summary><strong>DeFi market microstructure</strong><i>+</i></summary><p>AMMs, order books, MEV, decentralized protocols, tokenized assets and the structure of on-chain markets.</p></details>
          <details><summary><strong>Risk, market design and regulation</strong><i>+</i></summary><p>Robustness, surveillance, governance and the operational and regulatory challenges of AI in finance.</p></details>
        </div>
      </div></section>

